{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 45.141.215.17 attempted multiple malicious actions, including prompt injection attacks embedded in HTTP GET parameters and User-Agent headers to manipulate AI responses, alongside directory traversal attempts targeting sensitive AWS credentials. The logs also show failed SSH login attempts featuring secondary prompt injection payloads aimed at altering system operational modes. These techniques indicate a coordinated effort to bypass access controls and compromise application logic.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the source IP address 45.141.215.17 at the firewall and web application firewall (WAF).",
    "Implement strict input sanitization and validation on all query parameters and HTTP headers to neutralize prompt injection payloads.",
    "Review system and application access logs to ensure no unauthorized access to sensitive files like AWS credentials occurred."
  ]
}
